ProsperoSunshine: a profile the web page gives the game in front counts at once

The keyboard pad looks up the game in front every two seconds while the keys and mouse are in use, and reads
keyboard_profiles.txt only when that game changes (patch 0018). When the web page's Apps tab gives a title a profile
(SETKEYBOARD on the control socket, src/input/profile_list_edit.hpp), it sets prospero::profile_list_edited, and the next
look reads the list and picks the profile anew, for the game in front too. A list edited by hand still counts from the
next game on.

--- a/src/input.cpp
+++ b/src/input.cpp
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 #include "apps/titles.hpp"
 #include "input.h"
 #include "input/keyboard_pad.hpp"
+#include "input/profile_list_edit.hpp"
 #include "input/title_profile.hpp"
 #include "logging.h"
 #include "platform/common.h"
@@ -866,7 +867,8 @@
    * running title is sceLncUtilGetAppIdOfRunningBigApp's, so a suspended game keeps its profile in the console's menus,
    * and an app of the console's such as Settings is a title without one (keyboard_mouse_profile). The game is looked up
    * at most every two seconds while the keys and the mouse are in use, and its profile and the list anew only when it
-   * changes, so an edited list counts from the next game on.
+   * changes, so a list edited by hand counts from the next game on. One the web page changed (SETKEYBOARD on the control
+   * socket, prospero::profile_list_edited) counts within those two seconds, for the game in front too.
    *
    * @return The profile to play with.
    */
@@ -883,7 +885,8 @@
     checked = now;
     char running[16];
     const std::string in_front = ps_title_running(running) > 0 ? running : "";
-    if (in_front == title) {
+    const bool edited = prospero::profile_list_edited.exchange(false);
+    if (in_front == title && !edited) {
       return choice;
     }
     title = in_front;
